Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: opt in to direct UMA initial texture uploads

Simple initial color-texture uploads can avoid temporary staging allocations
on coherent UMA. Probe creation and initialization before constructing the DTL
resource, falling back only for unsupported operations. No existing resource
is replaced and no application data pointer survives the DDI call. Preserve
allocation/device-loss failures and keep this path opt-in pending GPU tests.

